&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;DEPT® is a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, our 4,000+ specialists deliver growth invention services across Brand &amp;amp; Media, Experience, Commerce, CRM, and Technology &amp;amp; Data. We’re 50|50 tech and marketing, partner-led, and first to move. Clients include Google, Lufthansa, Meta, eBay, and OpenAI. We have been certified B Corp and Climate Neutral since 2021.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JOB PURPOSE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a strategic and experienced Resource Manager to join our EMEA resourcing team for our Experience &amp;amp; Engineering DACH Team (Across Germany and Switzerland). This role is essential in ensuring efficient resource allocation, optimizing utilization, and aligning with business growth in a fast-paced digital environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be responsible for matching the right talent to the right projects - balancing team skills, availability, and project needs to deliver high-quality work, on time and on budget. This includes managing billable headcount, supporting dynamic staffing needs, and planning ahead with the Commercial team to align with the business pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A strong understanding of digital project delivery (e.g., websites, e-commerce, mobile apps) and the roles involved - such as UX/UI Design,Strategy, Engineers, QA, Devops, among others.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone with excellent people skills, an analytical mindset, and a proactive approach to team planning - someone who can help us operate with agility, elevate our talent, and support impactful client work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, you’ll work in a creative, fast-moving environment alongside brilliant minds, for a wide range of global clients. We value curiosity, growth, and a drive to make a positive impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resource Planning &amp;amp; Optimization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage the full resourcing lifecycle across Experience &amp;amp; Engineering requests for a pool of ~100 FTE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate capacity, utilization, and bandwidth to optimize allocation, balancing business needs with team wellbeing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make strategic resourcing decisions considering project margins, business priorities, and talent development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demand Forecasting &amp;amp; Workforce Planning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Sales, Delivery, Finance and Operation during project intake to build effective staffing plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain accurate short- and long-term demand forecasts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify skill gaps and workforce needs, partnering with Craft Leads and People &amp;amp; Culture on hiring and training.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Regional Resourcing &amp;amp; External Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate resourcing across EMEA, including nearshore and offshore teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and onboard freelancers or external partners when internal capacity is unavailable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a balanced approach between internal, nearshore/offshore, and freelance resourcing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a key partner to Delivery, Sales, Operations, Project Managers, and Craft Leads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure alignment between resourcing strategies and business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a consultative approach by advising on alternative profiles or staffing solutions based on project needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk Management &amp;amp; Conflict Resolution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify risks in resourcing plans and implement mitigation strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and resolve resource conflicts, competing priorities, and overlapping demands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting, Data &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high data quality within resource management tools (e.g., Resource Guru)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with processes such as time tracking, allocations, and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report on key metrics (utilization, capacity, bench, freelance/nearshore ratios)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular insights to local, regional, and global leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;ll BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in Resource Management, Engineering Resource Management, or Technical/Digital Project Management within a digital agency or product environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across multiple markets and cultures (EMEA experience is a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
